.TH "CSSTRANSFORMCOMPONENT.TOSTRING" "3JS" "September 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSTransformComponent.toString \- CSSTransformComponent: toString()
method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toString()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CSSTransformComponent\f[R] interface is a stringifier returning a
CSS Transforms function.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toString()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A string in the form of a CSS transform function.
.PP
This will use the value of \f[CR]is2D\f[R] to return either a 2D or 3D
transform.
For example, if the component represents \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] and
\f[CR]is2D\f[R] is false, then the string returned will be in the form
of the CSS transformation \f[CR]rotate3d()\f[R] function.
If true the string returned will be in the form of the 2\-dimensional
\f[CR]rotate()\f[R] function.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Serializing 2D and 3D components
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] translate2D = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20));
console.log(translate2D.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqtranslate(10px, 20px)\(dq\f[R]

\f[B]const\f[R] translate3D = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20), CSS.px(30));
console.log(translate3D.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqtranslate3d(10px, 20px, 30px)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
